 "title": "-vf subtitles Incorrect handling of .ASS wrapping margins",
 "body": "# Summary of the bug\n\nIn rare cases, the margins of a style (safezone), are off by at least one pixel.\nA line that should render as a 2-liner will render as a 3-liner with ffmpeg.\n![Screenshot 2025-09-22 033012](/attachments/b1057f87-911a-469c-a887-0fa7fbc01b93)\n![Screenshot 2025-09-22 033032](/attachments/251ab33c-51d2-4e3a-b99a-d4a4875852ab)\n![Screenshot 2025-09-22 033528](/attachments/516f361a-727c-49d9-9a52-3a89e1f03ade)\n# Steps to reproduce\nAegisub is required to view the subtitle directly.\nIt may also be necessary to load/install the font in order for Aegisub to display the text as intended.\n\nBelow I have provided a .zip which contains a muxed .mkv file containing the subtitle and font, which I also included externally, for convenience.\n\nTo reproduce the bug, execute following command and compare the resulting video with the preview in Aegisub.\n`%CD%`\n`ffmpeg -i blank.mkv -vf subtitles=blank.mkv hardsub.mp4`\n\nDecreasing the margins of the style by just 1 pixel (Left or Right), will result in a properly rendered line, confirming the issue.\n\nLog:\n[the 185 KB `-v 9` log was cut from this test fixture]",
